  "overview": "Roland and Rattfink is a series of animated shorts produced and released from 1967 to 1972. The main characters also made several guest appearances on The Pink Panther animated series. The series was produced by David H. DePatie and Friz Freleng. The cartoons concerned blond, good-looking, pacifist Roland and the many attempts by the evil, mustachioed Rattfink to ruin his good time. Roland and Rattfink were both voiced by Lennie Weinrib (except in \"The Deadwood Thunderball\" where they were voiced by John Byner and Dave Barry). \"Hurts and Flowers\" (one long, running joke about Rattfink destroying Roland's desires) concluded with Rattfink getting killed and Roland leaving daises on his grave. When Roland walked away, Rattfink's ghost rose from the grave to throw the flowers at him. Seventeen cartoons were produced.",
